{"id":"mahabharata-12-154","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":154,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 154 · The learned brahmin and self-control","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how a learned brahmin, eager for dharma, should act, and Bhishma says that the unrestrained man falls into trouble again and again. He says that the one who gives fearlessness to all beings is freed from the body.","kn":"ಧರ್ಮಾಸಕ್ತ ವಿದ್ವಾನ್ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಹೇಗೆ ನಡೆಯಬೇಕೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಇಂದ್ರಿಯ ನಿಗ್ರಹವಿಲ್ಲದವನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ತೊಂದರೆಗೊಳಗಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳಿಗೆ ಅಭಯ ನೀಡುವವನು ದೇಹದಿಂದ ಮುಕ್ತನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि धर्म के इच्छुक विद्वान ब्राह्मण को कैसे चलना चाहिए, और भीष्म कहते हैं कि असंयमी बार-बार कष्ट में पड़ता है। जो सब प्राणियों को अभय देता है वह देह से मुक्त हो जाता है।","te":"ధర్మాసక్తుడైన విద్వాంసుడైన బ్రాహ్మణుడు ఎలా నడుచుకోవాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; ఇంద్రియ నిగ్రహం లేనివాడు మళ్లీ మళ్లీ ఇబ్బందుల్లో పడతాడని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు. అన్ని జీవులకు అభయం ఇచ్చేవాడు దేహం నుండి విముక్తుడవుతాడు.","ta":"தர்மத்தை விரும்பும் கற்ற அந்தணன் எவ்வாறு நடக்க வேண்டும் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அடக்கமில்லாதவன் மீண்டும் மீண்டும் துன்பத்தில் விழுவான் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். எல்லா உயிர்களுக்கும் அச்சமின்மை அளிப்பவன் உடலிலிருந்து விடுபடுகிறான்.","ml":"ധർമ്മത്തിനായി ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്ന പണ്ഡിതനായ ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ എങ്ങനെ പ്രവർത്തിക്കണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; നിയന്ത്രണമില്ലാത്തവൻ വീണ്ടും വീണ്ടും ആപത്തിൽ വീഴുമെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. സർവ്വജീവികൾക്കും ഭയമില്ലായ്മ നൽകുന്നവൻ ശരീരബന്ധത്തിൽനിന്ന് മോചിതനാകുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.154; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"आपद्धर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Apaddharma Parva (Duties in distress)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स्वाध्यायकृतयत्नस्य ब्राह्मणस्य पितामह ।\nधर्मकामस्य धर्मात्मन्किं नु श्रेय इहोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, for a Brahmin who strives at private study and desires dharma, O righteous soul, what is said to be the highest good here?"}},{"n":2,"text":"बहुधादर्शने लोके श्रेयो यदिह मन्यसे ।\nअस्मिँल्लोके परे चैव तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a world of many views, tell me what you think is the best good here and in the next world, grandfather."}},{"n":3,"text":"महानयं धर्मपथो बहुशाखश्च भारत ।\nकिं स्विदेवेह धर्माणामनुष्ठेयतमं मतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great path of dharma has many branches, Bharata. Which of the dharmas is thought most fit to be practiced here?"}},{"n":4,"text":"धर्मस्य महतो राजन्बहुशाखस्य तत्त्वतः ।\nयन्मूलं परमं तात तत्सर्वं ब्रूह्यतन्द्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of the great and many-branched dharma, king, tell me without tiring what is its highest root in truth, dear one."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"हन्त ते कथयिष्यामि येन श्रेयः प्रपत्स्यसे ।\nपीत्वामृतमिव प्राज्ञो ज्ञानतृप्तो भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen, I will tell you how you will reach the highest good. Having drunk as it were nectar, you, wise one, will be satisfied with knowledge."}},{"n":6,"text":"धर्मस्य विधयो नैके ते ते प्रोक्ता महर्षिभिः ।\nस्वं स्वं विज्ञानमाश्रित्य दमस्तेषां परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sages have declared many rules of dharma, each relying on his own understanding; of them self-control is the final refuge."}},{"n":7,"text":"दमं निःश्रेयसं प्राहुर्वृद्धा निश्चयदर्शिनः ।\nब्राह्मणस्य विशेषेण दमो धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The old who see conclusions call self-control the highest good. For a Brahmin especially, self-control is eternal dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"नादान्तस्य क्रियासिद्धिर्यथावदुपलभ्यते ।\nदमो दानं तथा यज्ञानधीतं चातिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One without self-control does not properly attain success in actions. Self-control surpasses giving, sacrifices, and study."}},{"n":9,"text":"दमस्तेजो वर्धयति पवित्रं च दमः परम् ।\nविपाप्मा तेजसा युक्तः पुरुषो विन्दते महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Self-control increases radiance and is the highest purifier. A man free of sin and endowed with radiance gains greatness."}},{"n":10,"text":"दमेन सदृशं धर्मं नान्यं लोकेषु शुश्रुम ।\nदमो हि परमो लोके प्रशस्तः सर्वधर्मिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard of no dharma in the worlds like self-control; self-control is the most praised in the world among all who follow dharma."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रेत्य चापि मनुष्येन्द्र परमं विन्दते सुखम् ।\nदमेन हि समायुक्तो महान्तं धर्ममश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"After death too, best of men, he finds the highest happiness; one joined with self-control attains great dharma."}},{"n":12,"text":"सुखं दान्तः प्रस्वपिति सुखं च प्रतिबुध्यते ।\nसुखं पर्येति लोकांश्च मनश्चास्य प्रसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The self-controlled sleeps happily and wakes happily; he moves happily through the worlds and his mind is serene."}},{"n":13,"text":"अदान्तः पुरुषः क्लेशमभीक्ष्णं प्रतिपद्यते ।\nअनर्थांश्च बहूनन्यान्प्रसृजत्यात्मदोषजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One without self-control repeatedly meets affliction and produces many other misfortunes born of his own faults."}},{"n":14,"text":"आश्रमेषु चतुर्ष्वाहुर्दममेवोत्तमं व्रतम् ।\nतस्य लिङ्गानि वक्ष्यामि येषां समुदयो दमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the four stages of life, they say self-control is the best vow. I will tell you its marks, whose combination is self-control."}},{"n":15,"text":"क्षमा धृतिरहिंसा च समता सत्यमार्जवम् ।\nइन्द्रियावजयो दाक्ष्यं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forbearance, steadiness, non-violence, equanimity, truth, honesty, mastery of the senses, skill, gentleness, modesty, and steadiness of mind,"}},{"n":16,"text":"अकार्पण्यमसंरम्भः संतोषः प्रियवादिता ।\nअविवित्सानसूया चाप्येषां समुदयो दमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"freedom from meanness, from violent agitation, contentment, kind speech, absence of quarrelsomeness and envy: the combination of these is self-control."}},{"n":17,"text":"गुरुपूजा च कौरव्य दया भूतेष्वपैशुनम् ।\nजनवादोऽमृषावादः स्तुतिनिन्दाविवर्जनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reverence for the teacher, Kaurava, compassion for beings, freedom from slander, honest talk, and avoidance of praise and blame."}},{"n":18,"text":"कामः क्रोधश्च लोभश्च दर्पः स्तम्भो विकत्थनम् ।\nमोह ईर्ष्यावमानश्चेत्येतद्दान्तो न सेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Desire, anger, greed, pride, stiffness, boasting, delusion, envy, and contempt: the self-controlled does not practice these."}},{"n":19,"text":"अनिन्दितो ह्यकामात्माथाल्पेच्छोऽथानसूयकः ।\nसमुद्रकल्पः स नरो न कदाचन पूर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unblamed, free of desire, of few wants, and without envy, that man is like the ocean, which is never filled."}},{"n":20,"text":"अहं त्वयि मम त्वं च मयि ते तेषु चाप्यहम् ।\nपूर्वसंबन्धिसंयोगान्नैतद्दान्तो निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I in you, you in me, and I in them\": through past ties and connections, the self-controlled does not follow this."}},{"n":21,"text":"सर्वा ग्राम्यास्तथारण्या याश्च लोके प्रवृत्तयः ।\nनिन्दां चैव प्रशंसां च यो नाश्रयति मुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who takes refuge in no activity of village or forest in the world, nor in praise or blame, is freed."}},{"n":22,"text":"मैत्रोऽथ शीलसंपन्नः सुसहायपरश्च यः ।\nमुक्तश्च विविधैः सङ्गैस्तस्य प्रेत्य महत्फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is friendly, endowed with good character, with good companions, and free of various attachments gains a great fruit hereafter."}},{"n":23,"text":"सुवृत्तः शीलसंपन्नः प्रसन्नात्मात्मविद्बुधः ।\nप्राप्येह लोके सत्कारं सुगतिं प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of good conduct, endowed with character, serene in self, knowing the self and wise, gets honor in this world and attains a good destination."}},{"n":24,"text":"कर्म यच्छुभमेवेह सद्भिराचरितं च यत् ।\nतदेव ज्ञानयुक्तस्य मुनेर्धर्मो न हीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The good deed that is practiced here by the good: for the sage endowed with knowledge that very dharma does not decline."}},{"n":25,"text":"निष्क्रम्य वनमास्थाय ज्ञानयुक्तो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nकालाकाङ्क्षी चरन्नेवं ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going forth into the forest, endowed with knowledge and with senses conquered, awaiting his time, thus wandering, he becomes fit to merge with Brahman."}},{"n":26,"text":"अभयं यस्य भूतेभ्यो भूतानामभयं यतः ।\nतस्य देहाद्विमुक्तस्य भयं नास्ति कुतश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one from whom beings have no fear, and who has no fear from beings, once freed from the body there is no fear from anywhere."}},{"n":27,"text":"अवाचिनोति कर्माणि न च संप्रचिनोति ह ।\nसमः सर्वेषु भूतेषु मैत्रायणगतिश्चरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He neither piles up nor heaps up actions; equal toward all beings, he would walk the path of friendliness."}},{"n":28,"text":"शकुनीनामिवाकाशे जले वारिचरस्य वा ।\nयथा गतिर्न दृश्येत तथा तस्य न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the path of birds in the sky or of aquatic creatures in water is not seen, so is his, no doubt."}},{"n":29,"text":"गृहानुत्सृज्य यो राजन्मोक्षमेवाभिपद्यते ।\nलोकास्तेजोमयास्तस्य कल्पन्ते शाश्वतीः समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who leaves home and takes up liberation alone gains luminous worlds for everlasting years."}},{"n":30,"text":"संन्यस्य सर्वकर्माणि संन्यस्य विधिवत्तपः ।\nसंन्यस्य विविधा विद्याः सर्वं संन्यस्य चैव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Renouncing all actions, renouncing austerity as prescribed, renouncing the various kinds of knowledge, and renouncing everything,"}},{"n":31,"text":"कामेषु चाप्यनावृत्तः प्रसन्नात्मात्मविच्छुचिः ।\nप्राप्येह लोके सत्कारं स्वर्गं समभिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"not turning back to desires, serene in self, knowing the self, pure, he gains honor in this world and attains heaven."}},{"n":32,"text":"यच्च पैतामहं स्थानं ब्रह्मराशिसमुद्भवम् ।\nगुहायां पिहितं नित्यं तद्दमेनाभिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"That place of the Grandfather, arisen from the mass of Brahman, hidden in the cave, is reached by self-control."}},{"n":33,"text":"ज्ञानारामस्य बुद्धस्य सर्वभूताविरोधिनः ।\nनावृत्तिभयमस्तीह परलोके भयं कुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the enlightened one who delights in knowledge and is hostile to no being, there is no fear of return here, so how could there be fear in the next world?"}},{"n":34,"text":"एक एव दमे दोषो द्वितीयो नोपपद्यते ।\nयदेनं क्षमया युक्तमशक्तं मन्यते जनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In self-control there is one fault only, and no second: that people think the forbearing one weak."}},{"n":35,"text":"एतस्य तु महाप्राज्ञ दोषस्य सुमहान्गुणः ।\nक्षमायां विपुला लोकाः सुलभा हि सहिष्णुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"But for that fault, greatly wise one, the benefit is very great; for in forbearance wide worlds are easily won by the patient."}},{"n":36,"text":"दान्तस्य किमरण्येन तथादान्तस्य भारत ।\nयत्रैव हि वसेद्दान्तस्तदरण्यं स आश्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What use is the forest to the self-controlled? Nor to the unrestrained, Bharata. Wherever the self-controlled one lives, that is the forest and the hermitage."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"एतद्भीष्मस्य वचनं श्रुत्वा राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअमृतेनेव संतृप्तः प्रहृष्टः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words of Bhishma, King Yudhishthira was delighted, as if fully satisfied with nectar."}},{"n":38,"text":"पुनश्च परिपप्रच्छ भीष्मं धर्मभृतां वरम् ।\nतपः प्रति स चोवाच तस्मै सर्वं कुरूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he questioned Bhishma, best of those who uphold dharma, again, about austerity; and Bhishma told him everything, bull of the Kurus."}}]}]}